# Task 7 report — legacy-readiness descendant authentication

## Outcome

Task 7 is complete at commit `205df8d` (`Repair PIT readiness descendant authentication`). The required clean base was confirmed before editing. The only tracked production file changed was `core/pit_optimization_contract.py`.

The manifest builder now:

- retains canonical legacy-readiness authentication through `_authenticated_readiness`;
- requires the legacy readiness source commit to be a distinct local ancestor of the parity reference commit;
- rechecks that the parity reference commit is a distinct local ancestor of parity final;
- requires parity final head and tree fingerprint to equal the actual current clean source identity;
- seals that current identity, rather than the historical readiness identity, into the schema-v3 manifest.

The existing PIT bundle, baseline manifest, effective-policy, discovery-fold-manifest, and parity equality gates remain unchanged. Schema-v3 call/token limits, zero retries, `apply=false`, audit-only behavior, and create-only manifest writing were not changed.

